30. One subtle but very important point
Don't think:
"One eigenvector detects one specific semantic feature."
That's not necessarily true.
For example, in image PCA, PC1 does not automatically mean "scratch", PC2 does not automatically mean "dent", etc.
They are mathematically determined directions of maximum variance in the dataset.
Those directions may correspond to meaningful visual patterns, but PCA itself doesn't know the semantic meaning.
That's different from a supervised CNN, where learned features can become useful for classification/detection.
